# Copy to .env (NOT .env.local) and fill in once real values exist.
# The Prisma CLI reads .env only - a DATABASE_URL in .env.local produces
# "Environment variable not found" from a file that visibly contains it.
# Next.js reads .env too, so one file serves both. Both are gitignored.
#
# Every one of these
# is optional at build time - the site builds and runs correctly with none
# of them set (GA4/GSC wiring renders nothing; NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL falls
# back to a placeholder used in metadata/sitemap/robots).

# Canonical site URL, used in metadata, sitemap.xml, robots.txt, canonicals
# and every absolute URL in the structured data. No trailing slash.
# The domain is counterscent.com (renamed from parfumoza.com 2026-08-27 after
# a trademark-adjacent name collision; parfumoza was removed from Cloudflare
# 2026-09-10 and serves nothing). Set this the moment DNS points at the host -
# until then every absolute URL on the site emits an obvious placeholder,
# which is correct but must not reach production.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://counterscent.com

# GA4 measurement ID (e.g. G-XXXXXXXXXX). Leave unset and no GA script loads.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID=

# Google Search Console HTML meta-tag verification token. Leave unset and no
# verification meta tag renders.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GSC_VERIFICATION=

# NOTE: the public contact address (contact@counterscent.com, live since
# 2026-08-27) is NOT an env var. It is a constant in lib/site.ts, because a
# forgotten deployment setting would make /contact say "contact is not open
# yet" in production - worse than any alternative. Same reasoning for the
# site URL default above.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Marketplace / producer program
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THIS PROJECT HOLDS NONE OF THE MARKETPLACE'S ENV VARS ANY MORE. As of
# 2026-09-16 (build step 5), prisma/schema.prisma and neon.ts both moved to
# products/affiliate-sites/counterscent-producers/ - the producer console's
# own origin, which now exists and is the only place any code connects to the
# database. This project (the static catalogue) never did and still must
# never read DATABASE_URL: a paused or rotated database would fail the whole
# catalogue's deploy, and `output: "export"` gives it no server to read a
# credential from at request time anyway. See HANDOFF.md, "Run the export as
# a commit, not inside CI".
#
# If you are looking for DATABASE_URL, DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED, NEON_BRANCH, or
# the Neon setup notes: products/affiliate-sites/counterscent-producers/.dev.vars.example
# and that project's neon.ts and prisma/schema.prisma carry them now.
#
# What is still here: components/producers and lib/plans.ts, lib/producer-link.ts
# etc. - inert marketing pages and shared types with no API routes behind them
# (`output: "export"` means this project has none at all). lib/producer-session.ts
# is confirmed dead code (zero call sites) now that auth lives on the other
# origin; see its own header comment before touching it.

# Payment provider: PADDLE is the board's recommendation, and deliberately
# neither Stripe nor iyzico.
#   Stripe  - does not support Turkish accounts. The integration that once
#             lived here was deleted 2026-08-27.
#   iyzico  - capable of recurring billing, but the wrong shape for THIS
#             product: subscribers are US businesses, so a Turkish PSP means
#             FX friction on their side and leaves Sirketim as the seller of
#             record, owing US state sales tax, EU VAT and one e-fatura per
#             subscriber per period. It stays the right rail for Turkish
#             direct-invoice clients.
#   Paddle  - merchant of record, so it owes those taxes rather than us, and
#             our counterparty becomes one company with one document per
#             payout. Confirmed 2026-08-26 to onboard Turkish sellers.
# Open before any adapter is written: Paddle's marketplace acceptable-use
# policy, and whether it self-bills Turkish tax residents the way Awin
# explicitly does not.
# Nothing is needed here until a producer agrees to pay - the free tier
# requires no payment rail at all. It will land on the producer origin
# (counterscent-producers/), not here, when billing (build step 9) starts.
# See departments/accounting/reports/payment-rails-investigation.md.

# Local-only preview of the gated producer pages (/producers/submit), so the
# gated UI can be reviewed before authentication exists. Set to 1 and restart
# `npm run dev`.
#
# This CANNOT be enabled in a production build: lib/producer-session.ts also
# requires NODE_ENV === "development", which the bundler inlines at build
# time. An env-var-only switch here would be a genuine auth-bypass hole once
# this deploys. Pages using it render a visible preview banner.
PRODUCER_PREVIEW=
